### =========================================================================
### TicketHub — a walk through the whole API
### =========================================================================
###
### Open this file in Visual Studio or VS Code (with the REST Client extension)
### and click "Send Request" above each block. Run them in order: the login
### block sets the @token variable that everything below it uses.
###
### It is worth doing once end to end before reading the code — the shape of
### the API makes the layering much easier to follow.
### =========================================================================

@host = http://localhost:5048

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0 · Is it alive?
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/health

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1 · Sign in as the administrator
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The @login name captures the response so later requests can read
### {{login.response.body.accessToken}} without any copy-and-paste.
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@tickethub.local",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@refresh = {{login.response.body.refreshToken}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2 · Who am I?
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### No id parameter. The answer comes from the token, so it can only ever be
### about the caller — nothing to tamper with.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3 · Reference data
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/categories?pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The slim version, for a dropdown. Two fields instead of twelve.
GET {{host}}/api/categories/lookup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4 · Tickets — the filters
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Every one of these is optional and they compose. All of it becomes ONE
### SELECT — see TicketRepository.SearchAsync.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?page=1&pageSize=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortDescending=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Open and urgent
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?status=Open&priority=Urgent
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Past its SLA and not finished
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?overdue=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Nobody has picked it up
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?unassigned=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Free-text over title, ticket number and reporter name
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?search=pothole
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One department, newest first
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?departmentId=1&sortBy=createdAt
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5 · One ticket, in full
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Comments, attachments, history and rating — one query, all projected.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6 · Create a ticket
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Note what is NOT in the body: no status (always Open), no ticket number
### (generated), and no createdByUserId (taken from the token — see the
### mass-assignment warning on CreateTicketDto).
# @name created
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Fallen tree blocking the cycle path",
  "description": "A large branch came down overnight and is blocking the whole cycle path near the school.",
  "categoryId": 8,
  "priority": "High",
  "reporterName": "Nadia Haddad",
  "reporterPhone": "+970-59-555-1234",
  "reporterEmail": "nadia@example.com",
  "locationAddress": "Cycle path beside Al-Amal School",
  "latitude": 31.9522,
  "longitude": 35.2332
}

###
@newTicketId = {{created.response.body.id}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7 · Validation — these are SUPPOSED to fail
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Title too short + description too short → 400 with a field-by-field body.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hi",
  "description": "short",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "reporterName": "X"
}

### Half a coordinate. Attributes cannot catch this — it needs two properties at
### once, which is what Ticket.Validate (IValidatableObject) is for.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Coordinates that point nowhere",
  "description": "This request supplies a latitude but no longitude, so it should be rejected.",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "reporterName": "Test Reporter",
  "latitude": 31.9522
}

### Category that does not exist → 400. [Required] proved a number arrived;
### only the database can prove the number means something.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Category ninety-nine does not exist",
  "description": "The service checks this against the database before doing anything else.",
  "categoryId": 9999,
  "reporterName": "Test Reporter"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8 · The workflow
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Open → InProgress. Legal.
PATCH {{host}}/api/tickets/2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "InProgress"
}

### InProgress → Resolved. Also legal, and it stamps ResolvedAt.
PATCH {{host}}/api/tickets/2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "Resolved",
  "reason": "Crew attended and repaired the surface."
}

### Resolved → Open. NOT legal → 409, with a message listing what is allowed.
### The rule lives in TicketWorkflow.cs as a table, not as scattered ifs.
PATCH {{host}}/api/tickets/2/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "Open"
}

### Cancelling without a reason → 400. An audit trail with no reason is half an
### audit trail.
PATCH {{host}}/api/tickets/4/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newStatus": "Cancelled"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9 · Assignment
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/agents?hasCapacity=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Assign explicitly. Refused if the agent is in a different department or is
### already at their ticket limit.
PATCH {{host}}/api/tickets/2/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agentId": 2,
  "note": "Sara knows this street."
}

### Or let the server pick the least-loaded agent in the ticket's department.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/9/auto-assign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Un-assign: send null, and the ticket goes back in the queue.
PATCH {{host}}/api/tickets/2/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agentId": null,
  "note": "Back to the queue — Sara is on leave."
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10 · Comments
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A public comment — the reporter is notified.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "A crew is booked for Thursday morning. We will update you once it is done.",
  "isInternal": false
}

### An internal note. Staff only — a Citizen never receives this row, because
### the repository filters it out in SQL rather than trusting the front end.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Third complaint about this street this month. Worth flagging for resurfacing.",
  "isInternal": true
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 11 · Live chat over plain HTTP
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The same service the SignalR hub calls — two doors, one set of rules.
### For the real-time half, open http://localhost:5048/chat-demo.html
# @name conversation
POST {{host}}/api/chat/tickets/1/conversation
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@conversationId = {{conversation.response.body.id}}

### Saved, then broadcast to everyone connected — in that order.
POST {{host}}/api/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Hello — I am looking at your ticket now.",
  "clientMessageId": "11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
}

### Send the SAME clientMessageId again. Idempotent: you get the original
### message back rather than a duplicate.
POST {{host}}/api/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Hello — I am looking at your ticket now.",
  "clientMessageId": "11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555"
}

### History. Cursor paging, not Skip/Take — see ChatRepository.GetMessagesAsync.
GET {{host}}/api/chat/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/chat/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 12 · Notifications
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The badge. A COUNT, not a list you call .length on.
GET {{host}}/api/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 13 · Reports
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Grouped, averaged, sorted and paged in one query. No Rating row is loaded.
GET {{host}}/api/reports/category-satisfaction
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/reports/daily-volume
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/statistics
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 14 · The department boundary — the interesting one
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Sign in as Sara, a Roads agent.
# @name saraLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sara@tickethub.local",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

###
@saraToken = {{saraLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Roads tickets only. Not because she asked for Roads — because that is all
### the access filter will let the query return.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

### Ask explicitly for Sanitation (department 2) anyway. Still empty: the filter
### is applied BEFORE any caller-supplied filter, so it cannot be widened.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets?departmentId=2
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

### Ticket 4 is a Sanitation ticket. It exists, and for Sara it is a 404 —
### deliberately, because a 403 would confirm it exists.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/4
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

### Deleting is Admin only → 403. She is authenticated; the answer is still no.
DELETE {{host}}/api/tickets/1
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 15 · A citizen sees only their own
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name citizenLogin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "citizen@tickethub.local",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

###
@citizenToken = {{citizenLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Only the tickets Ahmad reported.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}

### Note the comment list: the internal note added in section 10 is NOT here.
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}

### Rating a resolved ticket he reported → works.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/5/rating
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stars": 5,
  "comment": "Sorted the next morning. Thank you."
}

### The same ticket again → 409. One rating per ticket, enforced by a unique index.
POST {{host}}/api/tickets/5/rating
Authorization: Bearer {{citizenToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stars": 1,
  "comment": "Trying to rate it twice."
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 16 · Registration and the token life cycle
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newcitizen@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "confirmPassword": "Passw0rd!",
  "displayName": "New Citizen",
  "phoneNumber": "+970-59-000-1111"
}

### Weak password → 400, with Identity's own messages passed straight through.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "weak@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "confirmPassword": "password",
  "displayName": "Weak Password"
}

### Refresh. The old token is consumed and a new pair issued (rotation).
# @name refreshed
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}"
}

### Present the SAME (now spent) refresh token again → 403, and EVERY session
### for that user is revoked. Reuse means a bug or a thief, and we cannot tell
### which — so we assume the worst. See AuthService.RefreshAsync.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 17 · Admin: user management
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Creates the login AND its Agent row, because an employee with no agent
### record cannot be assigned work.
POST {{host}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newagent@tickethub.local",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "displayName": "Yousef Darwish",
  "userType": "Employee",
  "roles": [ "Agent" ],
  "departmentId": 1
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 18 · Soft delete
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### The row is still in the table. The global query filter simply stops
### returning it — so the next GET is a 404 and the audit trail is intact.
DELETE {{host}}/api/tickets/{{newTicketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/tickets/{{newTicketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
